	"intro": [
		"Tailoring weaves cloth into bolts, then sews the bolts into cloth armour and bags. Cloth drops from humanoids, so it needs no gathering profession; Enchanting suits it, as the green pieces it makes break into enchanting materials.",
		"Ranks: Apprentice at any level from any Tailoring trainer (the first trainer teaches recipes only up to 55); Journeyman from level 10 at the city trainers; Expert from level 20 (50s) at Georgio Bolero in Stormwind or Josef Gregorian in Undercity; Artisan from level 35 at Timothy Worthington on Theramore Isle or Daryl Stack in Tarren Mill.",
		"Two patterns come from vendors: Runecloth Gloves (Qia in Everlook) and Runecloth Cuffs (Pexmit in Mount Hyjal). Past 280 only world-drop patterns from the Auction House reach 300: Runecloth Shoulders or Wizardweave Turban. The Loom patterns from Silithus would also do, but no town has a Loom."
	],
